{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>Like streams.</b> The tet has a dagesh because the nun of נטה is absorbed. For there are streams that incline this way and that, and upon them are trees." "<b>Like tents.</b> Like מר ואהלות (myrrh and aloes). And behold, he compared the tents to streams—\"they incline.\"" "<b>Like cedars.</b> Doubled in meaning. And he mentioned cedars as in ארז בלבנון ישגה (a cedar in Lebanon shall grow high)."], :book :numbers, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:19:16.615305216Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}